      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Before calling a plumber, you can try to clear the clog and remove the gross smell by pouring 1 cup of baking soda down the drain, followed by 1 cup of white vinegar. Let the mixture sit for a few hours or overnight, then rinse with hot water to see if the drain is flowing freely. You can also use a drain snake or plumbing auger to physically dislodge any blockages.",
